      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Outpouring of public grief for Lidia ‘Taty’ Almeida, leader of group of mothers that has marched every week since 1977</p><p>The human rights activist Lidia “Taty” Almeida – who spent more than half a century searching for her son after he was forcibly disappeared by Argentina’s military junta – has died aged 95, prompting a public outpouring of grief.</p><p>Almeida, 95, was the president of the Mothers of Plaza de Mayo, made up of women who have marched around the square outside Argentina’s presidential palace <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/apr/28/mothers-plaza-de-mayo-argentina-anniversary\">every Thursday since 1977</a>, demanding the return of children who were disappeared during the country’s 1976-1983 dictatorship.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jun/15/argentine-activist-taty-almeida-dies-disappeared\">Continue reading...</a>"
